    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0719" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1950v03/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/5–1050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State,
                        at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-05-10T16:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1950—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Tosec 157. Personal to the Secretary from Dulles.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d376-f1"
                    /> I have just read the text of Schuman’s statement regarding new political
                    authority to unify and administer German-French coal and steel resources. While
                    obviously many details lacking necessary for final judgment, it is my initial
                    impression that the conception is brilliantly creative and could go far to solve
                    the most dangerous problem of our time, namely the relationship of Germany’s
                    industrial power to France and the West. This proposal is along lines which
                    Secretary Marshall and I thought <pb facs="0720" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/> about
                    in Moscow in 1947 but which we did not believe the French would ever accept.
                    [Dulles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d376-f1" n="1" xml:id="d376-f1-content">
                <p>John Foster Dulles, Consultant to the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
